# The FMC controller driver.  It must be built in (=y), not a module: the
# rootfs lives on this controller, so a module would only load after the
# kernel had already failed to find its root.
#
# Stage A (probe + READ ID + the sysctrl breadcrumbs) lives in luofu-fmc.c;
# the register map, the command recipes and the vendor-vs-BSP poll decision
# are documented at the top of that file.

config MTD_NAND_LUOFU
	bool "Hisilicon luofu (Hi5671Y) FMC NAND controller"
	depends on ARCH_LUOFU || COMPILE_TEST
	depends on OF
	#
	# OUR ROUTE TO PSTORE_BLK.  In 5.10.201 `config PSTORE_BLK` carries `depends on BROKEN`, and
	# `config BROKEN` (init/Kconfig:116) is a PROMPTLESS bool - no prompt, so a fragment line
	# `CONFIG_BROKEN=y` is silently ignored and `olddefconfig` then DROPS PSTORE_BLK/MTD_PSTORE
	# with it.  Measured 2026-10-13: the symbols never reached .config and mtd10 stayed 0xff after
	# a full boot, which is indistinguishable from "the kernel died too early" - the whole reason
	# the persisted log was being built.
	#
	# `select` is the only mechanism that can set a promptless bool, and this symbol is ours and
	# always =y in our builds.  It is the route the fragment's own NOTE already named.  With BROKEN
	# selected, the fragment's CONFIG_PSTORE_BLK/CONFIG_MTD_PSTORE lines take, and the kernel
	# writes its console to the `pstore` mtd partition continuously - so a HANG leaves the log in
	# flash instead of dying with the box's RAM.
	#
	# BROKEN here only makes those symbols SELECTABLE; nothing else is selected by it.
	select BROKEN
	select PSTORE_BLK
	select MTD_PSTORE
	help
	  The flash memory controller of the Hisilicon Hi5671Y "luofu" SoC
	  (board R116, the Cudy WR3000 v2.0): a command engine plus a DMA
	  engine at MMIO 0x10a20000 driving the board's SPI-NAND on chip
	  select 1.

	  Stage A -- what this option builds today -- maps the controller,
	  resets the die and reads the chip ID, reporting each step through
	  the SoC's sysctrl scratch pair (0x10100c18/0x10100c1c) because the
	  board has no console.  It registers no mtd_info and cannot write to
	  the flash.  The page-read path and the MTD/SPI-NAND integration are
	  stage B.

	  Say Y here if you are building the luofu kernel.
